  "configuration_id": "config_041",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most critical question is whether the full multimodal pipeline with the strongest available encoders and aggregation can achieve high validation accuracy, establishing a performance ceiling for the remaining 9 experiments. config_041 combines scgpt (a purpose-built RNA foundation model, likely superior to PCA or scvi for capturing cell biology), imagenet_vit_l (the most powerful image encoder in the space), transformer aggregation (better than avgpool for modeling inter-profile interactions in multiprofile settings), and weighted fusion (allows adaptive balancing of modalities rather than fixed concatenation). This tests the hypothesis that the best-performing configuration lives in the 'strong encoder + sophisticated aggregation/fusion' region. If it performs well, subsequent experiments can explore whether cheaper components (resnet50, scvi_n200, avgpool) achieve similar accuracy at lower cost. If it underperforms, it localizes the problem to the interaction of these choices rather than a single weak component. Expected relative cost: highest in the search space (scgpt + ViT-L + transformer + multiprofile), but as experiment 1 it is justified to establish the upper bound; 9 experiments remain to explore cheaper alternatives."
}

